		       -----------------------
		       O88 NEW FEATURE HISTORY
		       -----------------------

Revision	Date		Product
--------	----		-------

3.00		11/1/87		O88
1.00		11/1/87		CC

	Major revision and new manual. Includes support for large
	case (option +B), use of very large I/O buffers (controlled
	w/+A), folding of string and floating-point constants (+F),
	debug support (+H), collapsing of JMP chains (+J),
	elimination of redundant code (+R), and PASCAL function call
	model (+S).  Incorporation of driver program, CC.EXE to
	simplify installation and use, especially with version 3
	release of C88.


3.01		1/1/88		O88.EXE

	Vastly extended	support for large case.


1.01		1/18/88		CC.EXE

	Added wild-card expansion capability. Source code filename
	can now be a filespec with '*' and '?' wildcard characters,
	in which case CC will compile all matching files.  If
	wildcards are used in the specification of the source
	file(s), then any simultaneous use of the '-o' option of C88
	must specify the name of a subdirectory rather than a file.


3.04		11/1/87		O88
1.02		11/1/87		CC

	NOTE: This new version 1.02 of CC now requires version
	      3.04 or later of O88!


    (a)	Added support for multiple source filespecs on command
	line, seperated by commas (and NO spaces):

		CC FILE1,WILD*.C,LASTFILE


    (b)	Added support for indirect files that contain one filespec
	(with optional wildcards) per line.  In the CC command line
	shown below, "FILELIST" is the name of a text file, and is
	indicated to be an indirect file by preceding its name with
	'@'.

		CC @FILELIST

	Indirect files may be used together with commas:

		CC FILE1,@FILELIST,OTHERS*.C


    (c)	Added +/-U (Update) options to CC:

		CC +U FILE

	Compares the time and date stamps of FILE.C and FILE.O
	(or filename specified with the -O option). Invokes C88
	to recompile the file if and only if the source (.C) file
	is newer (recently modified) than the object (.O) file.

		CC -U FILE

	Equivalent to +U, but only displays the commands that
	would be executed if +U had been specified instead.  In
	other words, -U shows you what files need to be recompiled.

	NOTE: This option MUST precede the filename, and the 'U'
	      must be preceded by a PLUS (+) or MINUS (-) sign.


    (d) Added ability to have CC do both compile and link:

    		CC PROGRAM=SRCFILE1,SRCFILE2,SRCFILE3

        The above command compiles the three indicated .C files
	and then executes BIND (or BBIND) to generate the .EXE
	file ("PROGRAM.EXE" in this example) whose name appears
	to the left of the equals (=) sign.

	This option is fully compatible with all other options.
	For example, if the object files are placed in another
	directory via the -O option, they will still be located
	properly for the BIND.  If the +/-U (Update) option is
	used, it should precede the name of the EXE file.


3.06		8/10/88		O88
1.04		8/10/88		CC

	Extended +F (Folding) so that it can now make substring matches.
	I.e., the string constant "xyz" would be mapped into a reference
	to the substring at the end of a string constant "abcxyz", instead
	of requiring an exact duplicate for folding.  Presently, the
	shorter substring must appear later in the data segment than the
	matching superstring.


3.06a		8/19/88		O88

	Simplified +7 in-line expansion of CALL _FCLEAR from
	FISTP WORD _FTEMP to FSTP ST(0).

	Added +7 in-line expansion of _FSTOREL, _FIS, and _FNOT.

	Added FLDPI, FLDL2T, FLDL2E, FLDLG2, and FLDLN2 to the 8087
	constant instructions (FLDZ and FLD1) that are generated by
	O88 to replace loading a constant from memory.  This provides
	a more accurate 80-bit representation of these constants to
	be generated internally by the 8087 rather than loading a
	less precise 64-bit constant from memory.  In order to
	do the replacement, O88 must find a 64-bit hexadecimal
	constant that matches one of the constants that can be
	generated by an 8087 instruction.  To be sure that the match
	is exact, you must code these constants in hex exactly as
	shown:

	#define	PI		((double) 0x400921FB54442D18)
	#define	LOG2OF10	((double) 0x400A934F0979A371)
	#define	LOG2OFE		((double) 0x3FF71547652B82FE)
	#define LOG10OF2	((double) 0x3FD34413509F79FF)
	#define	LOGEOF2		((double) 0x3FE62E42FEFA39EF)

	NOTE: Use of "PI" as defined above rather than the
	"PI" (and "PIO2") that are defined in PC Tech Journal's
	ACCURACY.C program, improved C-Ware's overall accuracy
	rating from 1.52 ("Poor") to 1.29 ("Fair"), or a 15%
	improvement.


3.06b		8/24/88		O88

	Added +7 in-line expansion of _FPUSH.

	Added +7 in-line expansion of log(), log10(), floor(),
	ceil(), and sqrt()

	Optimized the code generated when a function argument is
	a variable.  The new code uses 8088 PUSH instructions
	instead of an FLD followed by the expanded _FPUSH call.

	In-line expansion of 8088 and 8087 library routines is
	now dependent on +T (time optimization) as well as
	+E (expand some 8088 library routines), +M (expand
	_move and _lmove), and +7 (expand 8087 library routines).
	If time optimization is enabled (+T), then +E, +M, and
	+7 will expand their set of routines in-line as usual.
	However, if time optimization is disabled (-T) in favor
	of code space, only those +E, +M, and +7 routines that
	cause very little or no overall growth of the code
	segment will be expanded.

3.06c		9/6/88		O88

	Added optimization to replace:

		MOV r1,src1			MOV r2,src1
		SHL r1,1			SHL r2,1
		... (more shifts)	-by-	... (more shifts)
		MOV r2,r1			###

	Added in-line expansion (+E) for new C88 library functions:

		void _lset(unsigned off, unsigned seg, char c, unsigned n)
		unsigned _peekw(unsigned offset, unsigned segment)
		long _peekd(unsigned offset, unsigned segment)
		void _pokew(unsigned value, unsigned offset, unsigned segment)
		void _poked(long value, unsigned offset, unsigned segment)
		unsigned _rotl(unsigned value, unsigned shift_count)
		unsigned _rotr(unsigned value, unsigned shift_count)
